The analysis of 425924a reports scripts.check-runtime.server|site.table-key-not-checked.TYPES.ada29a86: "Lookup in `TYPES` can hit a built-in property. A key such as `constructor` returns a value that `TYPES` never held, and it is neither absent nor falsy." The test server in scripts/check-runtime.mjs picks a file's content type with TYPES[path.extname(file)], a plain object, so the result relies on no extension ever naming an Object.prototype member. In practice extname always begins with a dot, so this is defensive rather than a bug anyone has hit.

## What changed

scripts/check-runtime.mjs: computes the extension once and serves TYPES[ext] only when Object.hasOwn(TYPES, ext), otherwise application/octet-stream. Behaviour for every known extension is unchanged. This file is shared with none of the open agent PRs (#23, #24 and #34 cover the other three autofixable defects in this analysis: ENTITIES, MIME and the dropped boot() promise).

## How it was verified

`predictable fix-check` reported each of these defects gone, with no new finding, before this was proposed:

- `scripts.check-runtime.server|site.table-key-not-checked.TYPES.ada29a86` — the analysis reported 45 finding(s) before the change and 44 after

