The analysis of 425924a reports mcp.serve.__moduleInit__|site.async-work-in-void-slot.-.c47e47ad: "This async callback's work is never awaited. This callback returns before its work finishes..." node:http ignores the promise an async request listener returns. So if handleMcpRequest or sendWebResponse throws while someone runs `npm run mcp:serve`, the rejection goes unhandled: Node stops the local MCP server and the client is left with a hanging request.

## What changed

mcp/serve.ts: the request logic moves into handle(req, res). The listener calls it and catches any failure: it logs the error and answers 500 (or just ends the response if headers were already sent). Successful requests and the 404 path behave as before. Checked with tsc -p tsconfig.mcp.json. No open agent PR touches this file.

